**Thank you for using SEGUL!** 🙏🏻

**SEGUL (SEquence and Genomic UtiLities)** is a fast, memory-efficient tool for phylogenomic
datasets, from a few Sanger loci to thousands of loci across hundreds of samples. It runs on
phones, tablets, desktops, and computing clusters. For an independent review, see the
[Chan 2024 perspective](https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/full/10.1111/1755-0998.13993).

{% aside %}
The SEGUL CLI is on [Bioconda](https://anaconda.org/bioconda/segul) for Linux and macOS on
[ARM](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ARM_architecture_family) or
[x86_64](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/X86-64) CPUs:

```bash
conda install bioconda::segul
# or
mamba install segul
```

See [installing with conda](/docs/installation/install_cli/#conda).
{% /aside %}

## What's new

### SEGUI v1.2.0

The redesigned SEGUI app is available now on [Google Play](https://play.google.com/store/apps/details?id=com.hhandika.segui),
the [Microsoft Store](https://apps.microsoft.com/detail/SEGUI/9NP1BQ6FW9PW?mode=direct), and the
[Snap Store](https://snapcraft.io/segui), and rolling out to the App Store. See [GUI installation](/docs/installation/install_gui/).

- **New interface:** a searchable tool catalog, suggested workflows, and layouts for phones,
  tablets, and large screens.
- **New tools:** genetic distance, alignment trimming and unaligning, MAF conversion and summary,
  and sequence addition, filtering, and transposition.
- **Viewers and reports:** an alignment viewer for large alignments, and interactive reports for
  read, alignment, and distance summaries.
- **Inputs and outputs:** open folders and `.zip` or `.tar.gz` archives, and export output as
  archives.

See the [SEGUI release notes](https://github.com/hhandika/segui/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md#v120) for
all changes.

### SEGUL v0.25.0

- **Terminal viewers:** [`segul view align`](/docs/cli-usage/view-align/) opens alignments in an
  interactive viewer, and [`segul view summary`](/docs/cli-usage/view-summary/) browses summary
  reports as tables and charts.
- **Charts and reports:** summary commands write PNG or SVG charts with `--plot`.
  `segul align summary` and `segul align distance` also write JSON reports.
- **Read summary:** [`segul read summary`](/docs/cli-usage/read-summary/) adds read length N50,
  Q20 and Q30 bases, and, in complete mode, duplication, overrepresented sequences, and adapter
  content. It is about 12× faster in complete mode.
- **FASTQ input:** quality offsets and gzip or BGZF compression are detected from the reads, and
  PacBio HiFi quality scores are supported.

{% aside type="caution" %}
This release changes some `segul-core` read summary APIs. See the
[full release notes](https://github.com/hhandika/segul/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md#v0250) for all
changes.
{% /aside %}

